{"type":"tool_invocation","request_id":"request-1","attempt_id":"attempt-1","retry_of":null,"tool_call_id":"tool-1","duration_ms":40,"input":{"schema_version":"1.0","run_id":"c-rows","tool_call_id":"tool-1","tool":"read","arguments":{"source_id":"EV-S13","start":0,"end":1393}},"result":{"schema_version":"1.0","run_id":"c-rows","tool_call_id":"tool-1","tool":"read","status":"ok","data":{"span":{"source_id":"EV-S13","kind":"passage","start":0,"end":1393},"text":"# EV-S13 — Audit protocol\n\nFictional course data, issue #182. Date: 2026-11-14.\n\n## EV-S13:P01\n\nThis original fictional numerical extension uses method A (audit-a) as the daily-cost baseline and method B (audit-b) as the candidate. Both use the deterministic P01 shared-charger model and the same cost objective: penalties, charging and degradation, and deadheading. The costs are fictional cost units, not measured currency. We claim method B is 20% cheaper on the feasible paired subset, not on all logged runs.\n\n## EV-S13:P02\n\nPair only identical instance_id and run_id, represented by one pair_id. Require exactly one row of each method and both feasible=true. Reject ambiguous duplicate method rows. Exclude every row of an incomplete or infeasible pair; an infeasible cheap objective is not a valid daily plan. The CSV lists independent method executions within each paired deterministic day; experiment IDs identify executions, and EV-F-C identifies the comparison family.\n\n## EV-S13:P03\n\nUse the sum of method A costs as the denominator: reduction_ratio=(sum_A-sum_B)/sum_A; reduction_percent=100*reduction_ratio. Do not average per-pair percentages or divide by sum_B. Compare the percentage in percent with inclusive absolute tolerance 0.01 percentage points and relative tolerance zero. Costs, row identities, feasibility and pair membership are exact; ratio has tolerance 0.0001.\n\n"},"error":null},"schema_version":"1.0","run_id":"c-rows","event_id":"event-1","sequence":1,"elapsed_ms":74}
